-## Encode output is unchanged across the bump
+## Fix: bump to 2.3.1. Do NOT bump to 4.x as part of this.
 
-Encoding a representative index object under 2.3.0 and 4.1.1 produces **byte-identical** output. Despite spanning two majors, this bump does not churn the index format and does not require migrating existing boards. That is the main thing that makes it cheap; re-verify against a real index before landing rather than trusting this note.
